# 5. Data Model (Simplified MVP)

## User

* id (UUID)
* telegram_id (unique)
* level
* created_at

---

## Room (persisted in PostgreSQL)

* id (UUID or integer, stable)
* name
* topic
* **telegram_chat_id** — Telegram supergroup id (negative integer as stored by Telegram) used for all Bot API calls targeting that room’s group; must be set for moderation features to work.
* **invite_link** — current primary or tracked invite URL; **single source of truth in the DB**; may be **updated** after admin revokes/creates a link via the API (still stored only here, not duplicated in code config).

**MVP:** initial rooms (e.g. Travel, Dating, Business) are inserted via **Alembic migration** (seed data) or one-time seed step — not a standalone Python config file as the source of truth. Adding or backfilling **`telegram_chat_id`** is also done via **Alembic** when the schema is extended.

---

## Analysis

* id
* user_id
* transcript
* score (0–10)
* raw_response (JSON/text)
* created_at

